WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:07.210
MARKUS KLUTE: Welcome
back to 8.701.

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:11.350
So in this section, we look
at electroweak unification.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:13.510
So the aim is to
combine the weak

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:16.059
and the electromagnetic
interactions.

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:18.610
The issues we can
see here are first,

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:22.520
the strength of the
interactions are very different.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.070
This can be
mitigated by the fact

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:26.500
that we have heavy
gauge bosons involved,

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.590
and we have seen
our heavy particles

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:33.070
as being used as mediators
to kind of change

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.580
the strength of the interaction.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.710
So this might not
be a big issue.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:39.160
The second problem is that
the structure of the coupling

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.000
is very different.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.720
We have seen for QED that
they are the vector coupling

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.705
and for weak
interaction that they

00:00:46.705 --> 00:00:48.520
are the vector-axial coupling.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:53.440
This 1 minus gamma 5 is
vector minus axial coupling.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.970
So one way to
mitigate this problem

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:03.160
is to simply absorb this 1 minus
gamma 5 term in the definition

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:05.710
of the particle spinors.

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:08.180
And I have to warn you,
this is a little misleading.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:10.840
And I think that led also
to some of the confusion we

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.830
had in the class before.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:18.660
So what we are doing here
simply is, we take our spinor,

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:22.080
and we project out with
the 1 minus gamma 5 term

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.660
what the left-handed
component of this spinor is.

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:29.090
This is just a projection
and the definition of this.

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:32.480
And we can do this for
antiparticles as well as

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:35.750
for the right-handed
components as well.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:37.090
Good.

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:38.780
So now we can look
at the current again.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:43.340
And we look at this weak current
that you have seen you can

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:49.550
write as our antineutrino here,
gamma mu times 1 minus gamma 5

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:51.720
1/2 times e.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:02:00.270
Now, if we now define our
particles which gamma matrices,

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:03.150
we find that this
simplifies quite a bit,

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:06.660
because we now find the current,
which can be simply written

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.720
as a vector current.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:13.720
So we mitigated
this quite nicely.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:16.670
So what now happens to our
electromagnetic interaction

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:17.170
here?

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.840
So we have an electron
coupling to a photon.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.170
We can project out a
right-handed and left-handed

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:25.560
component, and then we have
to add them together again.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:31.440
When we do this, you
find that this component

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.960
of the left-handed
component, or the current

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.790
corresponding to the
left-handed particle

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:39.150
and the current corresponding
to the right-handed particle.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.610
There's no mixed
term here because

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:45.420
of the way gamma matrices or
gamma 5 matrices multiply.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:47.040
So that's nice.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:52.390
This also explains why the
helicity is not changed in QED.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:54.720
You basically see
this from the algebra

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.330
involved in those equations.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:57.890
Good.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:59.960
So far, we haven't
done anything.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:03.030
We have just changed
the notation.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.090
So we can go one step further.

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:08.450
And we use the
concepts we introduced

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:12.470
when we talked about QCD
or the strong isospin.

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:14.720
And since we can nicely
describe those currents here

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.480
of those particles,
we can maybe see

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:22.130
if we can write a
neutrino and an electron

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:24.320
as part of a duplet.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:27.560
And when we do this, we
rewrite the currents,

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.740
the positively charged and
the negatively charged current

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:37.805
as simply the left-handed
components of those duplets.

00:03:37.805 --> 00:03:41.510
We introduced a new matrix
here, tau plus and tau minus.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:45.020
And they're simply combinations
of tau 1 and tau 2,

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:46.910
which are, in fact,
the Pauli matrix.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.960
This is just a
relabelling as well.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:52.460
So there's a lot of relabelling
going on, not to confuse you.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.680
But we have simply
written this current

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:56.750
as positively
charged weak current

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.810
and negatively
charged current, where

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:04.190
we rotate a neutrino into
an electron or an electron

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:08.260
into a neutrino using
the weak interaction.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.040
Great.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:12.810
So now we can write
this current here

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:15.058
as the third component
of this current.

00:04:15.058 --> 00:04:17.100
And we see when we write
down the third component

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:20.610
of this current
using tau 3 here,

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.200
we find that something looks--

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.670
something which looks
like a neutral current.

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:27.630
So this is something like
a neutral current, where

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:30.240
we have a neutrino
coupling to a neutrino

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.980
and a left-handed
electron coupling

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.742
to a left-handed electron,
on a vertex vector

00:04:34.742 --> 00:04:37.820
[?] where there's an
interaction that was going on.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:40.940
This is not quite
the full story yet.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.220
Let me remind you
about the definition

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.380
we used also in
isospin, which is

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:51.650
the Gell-Mann-Nishijima
equation, which connected

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:54.710
the electric charge to the
isospin and the strangeness

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:55.470
of the particle.

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:56.720
And we do the very same thing.

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:00.200
We have an isospin component
and a so-called hypercharge

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:01.100
component.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.850
It's similar to the
strangeness we had before.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:08.600
And Q is the electric charge
of the particle involved.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:11.410
And so with this, we
can now define an iso--

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:15.180
a hyperspin current,
which is given as 2 times

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:18.050
the electromagnetic
current minus 2 times

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:22.490
the third component of the--

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:25.830
third component of
the weak current here.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:28.310
And so now we find
interesting effects here.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.830
There's a new component
which also couples

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.960
to right-handed particles.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:34.510
So the missing part here--

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:36.260
some of you might have
seen this already--

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:38.450
is this neutral current
in the upper equation

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:42.710
didn't connect or didn't
have a contribution

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.690
from right-handed particle.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.790
And since there's
right-handed electron which

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:50.450
coupled to Z boson,
there needed to be

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.050
this kind of additional term.

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:54.710
So now we have a
current which includes

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:57.510
the right-handed
particles as well.

00:05:57.510 --> 00:06:00.120
So that's great.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.850
We can generalize this
by writing those duplets

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:04.590
for all particles we know.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:06.660
There's an additional
kind of caveat here.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:08.750
We haven't talked
about this too much.

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:11.580
We have to consider the fact
that mass eigenstates are not

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.160
really the same eigenstates
which participate

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:15.670
in the weak interaction.

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:17.100
Right now we can ignore this.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.440
We'll later come back
to this question.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.240
And then we can write
the three components

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:28.260
of our isospin current and our
hypercharge current as well.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:33.670
Note that this EM current here
is our electromagnetic current.

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:34.170
Good.

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:38.280
So now we rewrote this, and
we find somehow very close

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:39.450
a consistent picture.

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:42.990
We find that there
is a charged current,

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:45.510
and then there is
a neutral current

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:47.830
in the weak interaction.

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:50.250
But what we actually
wanted to do

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:52.560
is combine the weak
interaction and

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:54.150
electromagnetic interaction.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:57.070
Now, let's look at this
again and start over again.

00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:59.812
So we have an
isospin current here,

00:06:59.812 --> 00:07:01.395
which copies to the
three components--

00:07:01.395 --> 00:07:04.960
the triplet, the
isospin triplet.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:10.320
So this is a W1, W2, W3 triplet.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:11.770
And then we have
the singlet here

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:15.780
which couples to
the hypercharge.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:17.100
Very good.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:21.510
So now, if I try to identify
now components which we already

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.460
know the first
thing we can do, we

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:28.860
have to make sure that we
find our W plus and W minus

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.250
bosons again.

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:32.310
And they're simply
linear combinations

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:35.650
of the W1's and the W2's.

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:37.150
And then the next
thing I have to do

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:40.150
is I have to find my
electromagnetic interaction.

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:46.120
And we can do that by binding
this A-- this is the photon--

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.790
as a linear combination
of the third component

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:52.420
of our triplet, isospin
triplet, and our singlet.

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:56.800
And what you see here
is that there's actually

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:57.860
mixing going on.

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:01.390
So we basically rotate those
with this mixing angle, which

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:07.150
we already introduced,
sine omega weak

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:09.520
mixing angle theta omega--

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:12.370
sorry, theta W.

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:14.320
So we find that the
photon can be made out

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:19.180
of a mixing of the third
component of the isospin

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:23.710
triplet and the
singlet component B mu.

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:27.160
And similarly, we
can find the Z boson

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:30.250
as the other component in this
mixing, the other state we

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:32.490
find in this mixing.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:34.510
The way we find
those mixings here

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:36.220
is through the couplings
we already know,

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:40.675
that we find this
omega g times sine

00:08:40.675 --> 00:08:47.230
theta W is equal to g
prime cosine omega W.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:51.100
And that's equal to the
electromagnetic coupling.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:55.600
And then similarly, we
find a solution for gz.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.570
So what we have seen now
is that apparently we

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:03.910
are able to combine the weak and
the electromagnetic interaction

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.500
by mixing--

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:10.630
by introducing the weak isospin
and by mixing isospin triplet

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:12.860
components with a
singlet component.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.770
And so we find a
picture which is

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:19.620
consistent with the W plus, a W
minus photon, and the Z boson.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.770
So that's very nice.

